Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:04.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Graph neural networks need many labeled nodes, and labeling is expensive.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.54,0:00:08.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This ICLR 2022 paper, Information Gain Propagation, rethinks graph active learning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.57,0:00:12.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Instead of asking an oracle for a node's exact class,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.61,0:00:16.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it asks a cheaper binary question: does this node belong to a given class?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.64,0:00:20.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}That soft label,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.68,0:00:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}plus a criterion picking nodes whose information gain propagates farthest,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.71,0:00:28.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}gives higher accuracy at lower cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.05,0:00:32.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Graph neural networks rely on large amounts of labeled data,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.84,0:00:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which is costly to obtain.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.48,0:00:39.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Active learning cuts this cost by selecting the most valuable nodes to label.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.35,0:00:44.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But every prior method assumes an oracle can always name a node's exact class.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.28,0:00:47.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}When categories are many or the domain is unfamiliar,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.63,0:00:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}that multi-class question is too demanding, and the budget is spent inefficiently.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.11,0:00:56.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Confirming a guess is far easier than naming the exact class.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.82,0:01:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}If an expert only answers a binary yes-or-no question,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.54,0:01:04.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the labeling cost per node drops sharply, especially with many classes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.25,0:01:07.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Meanwhile,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.96,0:01:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}existing selection criteria were built for hard labels and only measure a single node's uncertainty.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.67,0:01:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}They ignore that in a graph network,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.39,0:01:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}labeling one node propagates supervision across its k-hop neighborhood.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.40,0:01:22.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The paper makes three contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.53,0:01:25.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.65,0:01:28.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a new active-learning paradigm for graph networks that uses relaxed queries and soft labels
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.78,0:01:31.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}instead of exact-class annotation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.91,0:01:34.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.03,0:01:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a node-selection criterion that maximizes how information gain propagates through the graph.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.16,0:01:41.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.28,0:01:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}experiments showing it beats state-of-the-art baselines and generalizes across many graph neural network backbones.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.71,0:01:48.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}IGP runs in a loop.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.30,0:01:51.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A graph network is first trained on the labeled nodes with their soft labels.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.89,0:01:55.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For each candidate, the oracle is asked only whether the predicted label is correct,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.47,0:01:58.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and that answer becomes a normalized soft label.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.06,0:02:02.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To choose nodes,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.65,0:02:06.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}IGP measures how strongly each node influences its neighbors through propagation,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.24,0:02:09.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the influence magnitude, and combines it with the information gain,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.83,0:02:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the entropy reduction, of every influenced node.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.41,0:02:16.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It then selects the budget-limited subset that maximizes total propagated information gain,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.00,0:02:20.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}updates the model, and repeats.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.89,0:02:26.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}IGP is evaluated on five graph benchmarks: the citation networks Cora, Citeseer,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.30,0:02:29.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and PubMed, the large social network Reddit,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.28,0:02:32.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the Open Graph Benchmark dataset ogbn-arxiv.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.53,0:02:37.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Crucially, the budget is defined as true annotation cost, not a count of labels,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.94,0:02:41.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}since an exact query is far pricier than a binary one.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.59,0:02:44.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Budgets vary from two to twenty labels per class.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.21,0:02:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Across every dataset and budget, IGP delivers the highest test accuracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.77,0:02:56.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Under twenty labels per class with a GCN, it reaches 86.4 percent on Cora,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.48,0:03:02.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}75.8 on Citeseer, and 83.6 on PubMed, beating the strongest prior method, GRAIN,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.66,0:03:05.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}by 1.6 to 2.2 percent on citation networks,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.98,0:03:10.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with smaller but consistent gains on Reddit and ogbn-arxiv.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.53,0:03:16.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}As budget grows, IGP climbs fastest, and the lead holds across backbones.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.47,0:03:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}An ablation disables one component at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.60,0:03:24.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Removing informative selection, the propagation-aware node choice,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.19,0:03:27.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}causes the largest drop, up to 3.2 percent on PubMed,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.88,0:03:30.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}making it the most important ingredient.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.66,0:03:35.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Removing informative training with soft labels costs up to 2.9 percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.61,0:03:39.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}dropping the influence-magnitude information quantity up to 2.1,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.06,0:03:43.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and removing the normalized label up to 2.4.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.12,0:03:44.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Every piece contributes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.09,0:03:48.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The headline numbers: 86.4 percent accuracy on Cora,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.57,0:03:51.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a 2.2 percent gain over the best baseline,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.37,0:03:55.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}state-of-the-art results across five datasets and four GNN backbones,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.99,0:04:02.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}all achieved by replacing the expensive exact-class question with one cheap binary query per node.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.84,0:04:04.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The takeaway is simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.36,0:04:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Ask a cheap binary yes-or-no question,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.87,0:04:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and select nodes whose information gain propagates farthest across the graph.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.96,0:04:16.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}IGP makes graph active learning both more accurate and far cheaper to label,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.98,0:04:19.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and works with any graph neural network.
